{
    "_comment": [
        "Root-only development patches, carried by uams-web/patches-pest-plugin-mutate and listed here in the package's order.",
        "Each is temporary; the package retires them. Retirement of the function-default patch: UAMS-Web/uams-2020#673."
    ],
    "patches": {
        "pestphp/pest-plugin-mutate": {
            "Launch each mutant child process so a run cannot score every mutant killed without executing one (temporary; see #2322)": "vendor/uams-web/patches-pest-plugin-mutate/patches/pest-plugin-mutate-mutant-process-launch.patch",
            "Stop three silent @pest-mutate-ignore parsing defects suppressing nothing or the wrong set (temporary; see #2327)": "vendor/uams-web/patches-pest-plugin-mutate/patches/pest-plugin-mutate-annotation-parsing.patch",
            "Let a mutant child on Windows run its tests and write files, so its failure is a real kill (temporary; see #2524)": "vendor/uams-web/patches-pest-plugin-mutate/patches/pest-plugin-mutate-windows-mutant-child.patch",
            "Drop the run's own --filter from each mutant child so a filtered run cannot score every mutant killed (temporary; see #2570)": "vendor/uams-web/patches-pest-plugin-mutate/patches/pest-plugin-mutate-drop-run-filter.patch",
            "Widen or refuse a mutant child's filter that PCRE cannot compile, or that would pass cmd.exe's command-line limit on Windows, so it cannot score a kill without running a test (temporary; see #2578, #3114)": "vendor/uams-web/patches-pest-plugin-mutate/patches/pest-plugin-mutate-windows-filter-length.patch",
            "Create the mutations directory and fail on a mutated source that cannot be written, so a run cannot score mutants it never applied (temporary; see #2812)": "vendor/uams-web/patches-pest-plugin-mutate/patches/pest-plugin-mutate-write-mutated-source.patch",
            "Drop the parallel runner's options (--passthru-php, --processes and the rest) from each mutant child so a parallel run given one cannot score every mutant killed (temporary; see #2926, #2947)": "vendor/uams-web/patches-pest-plugin-mutate/patches/pest-plugin-mutate-drop-parallel-runner-options.patch",
            "Select tests for a mutated scalar function default, so it is not scored without a test running it (temporary; see UAMS-Web/uams-2020#673)": "vendor/uams-web/patches-pest-plugin-mutate/patches/pest-plugin-mutate-function-defaults.patch",
            "Propagate a mutation into isolated test processes and reject a test report that ran no tests, so an isolated run cannot score a mutant killed without running a test (temporary; see UAMS-Web/UAMSWP-Logo-List#82)": "vendor/uams-web/patches-pest-plugin-mutate/patches/pest-plugin-mutate-isolated-processes.patch",
            "Map a class constant mutant to the tests covering its containing class, since a constant initializer has no executable coverage line (temporary)": "vendor/uams-web/patches-pest-plugin-mutate/patches/pest-plugin-mutate-class-constant-coverage.patch",
            "Skip a node whose own comment carries a matching @pest-mutate-ignore marker, including when the traverser still leaves that node (temporary)": "vendor/uams-web/patches-pest-plugin-mutate/patches/pest-plugin-mutate-ignore-annotated-statement.patch",
            "Size a mutant child's time limit from the serial work the initial suite stands for, so a --parallel run cannot score a mutant a timeout that no test caused (temporary; see UAMS-Web/patches-pest-plugin-mutate#2)": "vendor/uams-web/patches-pest-plugin-mutate/patches/pest-plugin-mutate-mutant-timeout.patch"
        }
    }
}
